# lean-dev rules for Cursor

## Model Usage

Match the model to the task:
- File search, grep, read-only tasks: use the fastest/cheapest model
- Planning and analysis: use the mid-tier model
- Writing and editing code: use the mid-tier model
- Complex refactors and architecture decisions: use the most capable model

## Session Discipline

- One task per conversation
- Start a new chat when switching to an unrelated task
- Prefer specific file:line references over broad exploration
- After significant changes, start a fresh conversation

## Response Style

- Keep responses focused on the task at hand
- No unnecessary explanations or summaries
- Reference specific files and line numbers
- Don't re-read files already in context

## Code Style

- Match existing patterns in the file being edited
- No comments explaining what the code does
- No features, refactors, or abstractions beyond what was asked
- No error handling for scenarios that can't happen
